(367754, 29389, 772, '<td valign="top">beautiful work... i love the ''surrealism'' provided by this image... the light.. the dark... the ''contrast'' is excellent.  There are a lot of great images in this challenge, but this is one of the few that works its way to the top of my list... excellent work... = 10</td>', 'beautiful work... i love the ''surrealism'' provided by this image... the light.. the dark... the ''contrast'' is excellent.  There are a lot of great images in this challenge, but this is one of the few that works its way to the top of my list... excellent work... = 10', '2003-07-27 14:30:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(367755, 29701, 772, '<td valign="top">simple... great contrast... excellent idea as well.  I don''t really have much to offer you in the way of a comment here other than I really like the image.  = 10</td>', 'simple... great contrast... excellent idea as well.  I don''t really have much to offer you in the way of a comment here other than I really like the image.  = 10', '2003-07-27 14:31:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(367757, 29663, 772, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful abstract.  I love the shapes and texture here as well as the contrast.  This photo is also a great example of where some minor spot editing capabilities would allow you to ''finish'' the work for use in a challenge :)  I know how difficult and frustrating this can be... still gets a 10 from me... great work :)</td>', 'This is a beautiful abstract.  I love the shapes and texture here as well as the contrast.  This photo is also a great example of where some minor spot editing capabilities would allow you to ''finish'' the work for use in a challenge :)  I know how difficult and frustrating this can be... still gets a 10 from me... great work :)', '2003-07-27 14:34:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(367796, 29492, 5728, '<td valign="top">I would have cropped out the grass at the bottom of your image, otherwise a good photo.</td>', 'I would have cropped out the grass at the bottom of your image, otherwise a good photo.', '2003-07-27 16:05:29.000000', NULL, 1),
