(370329, 29582, 2586, '<td valign="top">I had no illusions about this submission whatsoever. The moment i decided that the most suitable gallery for it would be Digital Art, i knew i was in trouble :) Anyway, i had fun doing this. <br/> <br/>I like digital art. What i don''t like is pictures posturing as photographs because they had some cheap and easy photoshop gimmicks, beyond normal post-processing, applied to them. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-31 12:01:19.</i></td>', 'I had no illusions about this submission whatsoever. The moment i decided that the most suitable gallery for it would be Digital Art, i knew i was in trouble :) Anyway, i had fun doing this.  I like digital art. What i don''t like is pictures posturing as photographs because they had some cheap and easy photoshop gimmicks, beyond normal post-processing, applied to them. ', '2003-07-30 03:24:03.000000', '2003-07-31 13:01:19.000000', 0),
(371543, 29567, 8727, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the helpful comments.  I''ve got a lot to learn; when the opportunity presented for a definite contrast, I snapped eventhough the UV rate was 10+.  I''ve been reading some of the tips on resizing, but I''m afraid I still haven''t got the hang of it.  Any pointers would be greatly appreciated.</td>', 'Thanks for all the helpful comments.  I''ve got a lot to learn; when the opportunity presented for a definite contrast, I snapped eventhough the UV rate was 10+.  I''ve been reading some of the tips on resizing, but I''m afraid I still haven''t got the hang of it.  Any pointers would be greatly appreciated.', '2003-07-30 18:55:38.000000', NULL, 0),
